repository-artifact: "https://pypi.org/project/nn-dataset/"
url: "https://github.com/ABrain-One/nn-dataset"
abstract: >-
  LEMUR (Learning, Evaluation, and Modeling for Unified Research),
  distributed on PyPI as nn-dataset, is an open-source Python
  framework for training neural networks and analyzing their results
  under a shared protocol. Researchers provide model code and select
  a task, dataset, and evaluation metric; the framework trains the
  model and records its scores, losses, hardware context, and
  resource use at every epoch in a queryable database. Additional
  analyses characterize layers and identify architectures from source
  code, so results from different studies can be compared. Models,
  data loaders, transformations, and metrics are added as individual
  Python files, and a programmatic interface accepts a network's
  source code and returns validated measurements, allowing AutoML and
  code-generation systems to submit candidates without manual
  intervention.
keywords:
  - Python
  - PyTorch
  - deep learning
  - neural network dataset
  - neural architecture search
  - AutoML
  - hyperparameters
  - benchmarking
  - experiment management
  - reproducibility
  - LLM integration
